<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis of Mousson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1073</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis of Mousson was an 11th-century nobleman who held the county of Montbéliard and, through his marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophie-of-bar">Sophie of Bar</a> around 1038, the county of Bar. Their descendants, the house of Montbéliard-Bar, ruled Bar as a separate principality between Champagne and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. His lands guarded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belfort-gap">Belfort Gap</a> between the Jura and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vosges">Vosges</a>.</p></div>
